== Notes ==
* If any variant floors were encountered during descent, all floors of the Ascent will still be the original ones. For example, if the second floor on a run was the {{s|Cellar}} II or the {{s|Burning Basement}} II, during the Ascent, it will be replaced by the {{s|Basement}} II regardless. This includes alternate chapters, such as the {{s|Downpour}}, and so on.
** However, it's still possible to access them through the use of [[Debug Console]].
* Isaac won't encounter any [[curse]]s during the Ascent, except {{cu|Labyrinth}} if it was on the original floor.
** When encountering {{cu|Blind}}, it may be a good idea to skip boss and treasure room items, as they will be revealed during the Ascent.
** XL floors in the Ascent will contain both {{r|Treasure Room}}s from the original floor.
* Red {{r|Treasure Room}}s found through the {{i|Red Key}} during the original run will automatically show up during the Ascent, and will be adjacent to normal rooms. These doors do not require keys to open.
* Any unopened {{r|Treasure Room}}s on previous floors will still be locked during the Ascent.
** If these skipped Treasure Rooms are entered during the ascent, they will contain different items. This is best viewed with the effect of {{I|Dream Catcher}}.
** This also means a strategy is to skip {{r|Treasure Room}}s early in a run to spawn a {{r|Planetarium}}, and then get the skipped Treasure Room items during the Ascent. However, there's no need to keep doing it after encountering a Planetarium, since the probability to encounter it will stay at 1%.
* {{r|Angel Room}}s and {{r|Devil Room}}s will have different contents than on the original path.
** Since the {{r|Boss Room}}s have already been cleared during descent, Devil Rooms and Angel Rooms won't open during the Ascent, and can only be accessed with teleport effects.
** The special Angel Room Shops generated by {{I|The Stairway}} will also have different contents.
* During the Ascent, both items in a double item {{r|Treasure Room}} are visible.
* Items and trinkets that activate on entering the floor, such as {{T|Maggy's Faith}}, will trigger each time Isaac ascends a floor.
* If pickups were transported to another floor from the Treasure or Boss Room by {{t|Myosotis}}, their copies will remain in those rooms and can be encountered during the Ascent. Affected trinkets still transform into {{p|Cracked Key}}s, potentially allowing you to gain large amounts of Cracked Keys.
** {{T|Myosotis}} will work on the Ascent, and can be used to bring an additional pickup if holding a {{p|Cracked Key}}.
* In each floor, after exploring all normal rooms, using {{I|Teleport 2.0}} will teleport Isaac to the {{r|Angel Room}}/{{r|Devil Room}}, since {{r|Secret Room}}s and {{r|Super Secret Room}}s will not spawn.
* If a floor is restarted, which can be accomplished through using {{I|Forget Me Now}} or by finding a Red 5-pip {{r|Dice Room}}, the following effects will happen:
** No dream animations will be shown when restarting.
** The regenerated floor will still be an Ascent floor, not a descent floor.
** If the floor was an XL one, the regenerated floor will also be XL.
** If the {{r|Treasure Room}} was skipped during descent, and during the Ascent its contents were seen, after restarting it will contain different items.
** All {{P|Cracked Key}}s in either the {{r|Boss Room}} or the {{r|Treasure Room}} will remain there, even if they were used before restarting.
* The {{r|I AM ERROR}} room can be reached during the ascent. {{r|I AM ERROR}} rooms will mimic the layout that they had corresponding to the floor. Rather than containing a trapdoor, they will contain a beam of light leading up to the next floor.
* Entering an {{r|I AM ERROR}} room in {{s|Gehenna}} II (before the Ascent) takes Isaac to the starting room of the floor.
* No consumable voice lines will be spoken during the Ascent.
* {{C|Jacob and Esau}} will overlap one other when ascending to a new floor. This effect stops upon pressing the Swap key or entering a new room.
* During the descent, it is recommended to leave any abandoned [[Trinket]]s in {{r|Treasure Room}}s or {{r|Boss Room}}s, so that the resulting {{P|Cracked Key}}s can be used during the Ascent, which could potentially create special rooms containing items or other useful pickups.
* If the Boss Music would play, it plays the Boss Music for the alternate path rather than the Boss Music for the main path. One way to make Boss Music play is to find an Angel Room by using a {{i|Red Key}}/{{p|Cracked Key}}.
* If a Boss is not fought during the descent (e.g. if it was skipped using {{i|We Need To Go Deeper!}}), the {{r|Boss Room}} will still be empty during the Ascent.
* Portals to {{s|The Void}} that spawn after the {{e|Mom}} fight will still appear in the boss room during Ascent, however they will be permanently closed.

